2 CONT Posted to my Geni public Profile Comments Thread.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Prof. Antonio de Sotomayor, Ph.D. December 24, 2015 at 6:49 PM 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hello Theresa. Ana de Lugo Sotomayor (wife of Diego Montañez de Sierra) was the daughter of Captain Don Juan de Lugo Sotomayor (bc 1590, San Juan) and Doña Luisa Velásquez (bc. 1592, San Juan). Don Juan de Lugo Sotomayor was the s
2 CONC on of Don Pedro Mexia de Lugo (bc. 1565, San Juan) and Doña Isabel de Sotomayor y Pérez del Rincón (bc. 1570, San Juan). The possible conection here would be Doá Isabel de Sotomayor, but she inherited her surname Sotomayor from an
2 CONC  ancestor (possible a grandmother or great grandmother) because her parents were Don Herán Pérez de Valenzuela and Doña María del Rincón. Sometimes daughters would inherit surnames from female ancestors as an act of respect and ho
2 CONC nor. Don Hernán's parents were Don Alonso de Lepe and Doña Catalina Perez. Don Hernán and his parents were from Almonte, Andalucía, Spain. The Sotomayors are one family and descend from Men Paes de Sorred who was granted the Lords
2 CONC hip over the valley of Souto in Pontenvedra, Galicia in the 1100s by King Alfonso VI and named it Souto Maior (Great Grove). All the Sotomayors descend from this man, but many have inherited the lastname through female lines, like
2 CONC  the case of Isable illustrate. I hope this helps. Merry Christmas!"
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is the profile, he was looking at, too, when he formulated this. One of my 6th great grandfathers. ~Theresa Renée Delgado-Tossas<br/>
2 CONT
