2 CONT Antonio Ramírez de Arellano Figueroa (son of Lázaro Ramírez de Arellano Benavides and Clara de Figueroa Vargas)241 was born 04 Mar 1653, and died date unknown. He married Ana Lugo y Sotomayor in San German, Puerto Ríco.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Includes NotesNotes for Antonio Ramírez de Arellano Figueroa: Book: Familias de Cabo Rojo -Enrique Ramírez Brau tried to establish who was the father of Remigio. -According to Mr. Acosta, there is no documented proof, but agrees 
2 CONC with Mr. Brau that Remigio was the son of the well known "Corregidor de San Germán" Antonio Ramírez de Arellano. -Mr. Brau found some documentation with testimonies of several neighbors of San Germán,  regarding the parents and gr
2 CONC andparents of Antonio as; Lázaro Ramírez de Arellano,  already dead in 1693- the date of the testimony, and Clara de Figueroa. -Ms. Acosta also states that on a personal conversation with Lluch Mora, he mentioned that Antonio Ramí
2 CONC res de Arellano (Capitán y Teniente a Guerra) reched to the rank of Brigadier General. -In that conversation, she states they discussed that Ana Lugo, Antonio´s wife,  was also from the Buenaventura & Sotomayor. -Antonio was also 
2 CONC defender of the Island from the governor of the Island of Tortuga,  Monsieur Beltran D'Oregon. -D'Oregon invaded the island in Piñales, near the Añasco River in 1673. -Antonio was born on the 4th of March, 1653 & won the battle ag
2 CONC ainst D'Oregon in Piñales when he was only 20 years old. Source: Ursula Acosta & David E. Cuesta Camacho, Familias de Cabo Rojo, (1st Edition, 1983). Pg 91
2 CONT
2 CONT May 21, 2006 I found this article on my notes from Dr. Ursula Acosta´s notes published on her website.
