2 CONT  Includes NotesMarriage Notes for Antonio Ramírez de Arellano Figueroa and Ana Lugo y Sotomayor: Book: Familias de Cabo Rojo -Dr. Acosta states that Brau listed these as the children of Antonio & Ana. Eugenio- Married to María del
2 CONC  Rosario martínez de Matos Germán- Married to Teresa Pabón Dávila Esteban- María del Toro y Quiñones Juan- Married to Ana Martínez de Matos y Espinosa Sebastián- Married to Juana de Mirabal Pedro- Married to Margarita Benavides Pe
2 CONC tronilla- Married to José Ramos Colón Andrés- Married to Juana de Rivera Juana- Married to Baltazar Sepúlveda and possibly Laurencio- Married to Antonia Martínez de Matos -Dr. Acosta makes a point that Petronila cannot be the sist
2 CONC er of Remigiuo, but a cousin. In the marriage of Valentín Ramírez de Arellano with María Belén Ramírez de Arellano in 1819 in Cabo Rojo, she concludes that the Great-Grandmother of Valentín, Petronila, & the Great- Grandfather of 
2 CONC Marís Belén, Eugenio...were brothers.It indicates that Petronila was first cousin to the son of Eugenio (2º with 3º grados de Consanguinidad)- Petronila being the niece of Eugenio. -Another evidence she found that proved Petronila
2 CONC  is not a sister, but a niece to Remigio, is that ifPetronila is a niece of both Remigio and Eugenio- they they must be brothers.She believes there may have been a mistake in the redording of the Consanguinity in the marriage of 1
2 CONC 819, having to do with the Great Grandparents of the bride and groom. -She concludes that Antonio has the following children: RemigioJuanEugenioEstebanJuanaLaurencio and possibly these... -Baltazar-Sebastián-Pedro-Andrés Also that
2 CONC  Germán was a first cousin, and Petronila is the niece of Remigio & Eugenio & not a sister. Source:Ursula Acosta & David E. Cuesta Camacho, Familias de Cabo Rojo,(1st Edition, 1983). Pg 92-93 Children of Antonio Ramírez de Arellan
