0 @N6000000005024488358@ NOTE Catholic
1 CONT The Norman adventurer Jean de Bethencourt "The Great" first conquered the Canary islands of  in 1402. He is the proginator of the Bethencourt name which has since undergone several variations including Betancur.
1 CONT
1 CONT Conquest (of the Canary Islands) in earnest only began with the Norman adventurer Jean de Bethencourt who, in 1402 , claimed Lanzarote on behalf of his feudal lord. Henry III of Castile. 
1 CONT
1 CONT All Betancur (and other spelling variations of Bethencourt) families of the Canaary Islands are descended from the Norman French Bethencourt family of Jean de Bethencourt.
0 @N6000000000374551305@ NOTE BIOGRAPHY: Alguazil-mór do Santo Ofício da Inquisição
